  "body": {
    "title": "Shared process lifecycle and spawnManaged",
    "summary": "In shell-helper.ts add one lifecycle: effective signal tested before spawn, own process group on non-win32, group kill on abort/time-out/stderr overflow, 2 s bounded settlement destroying streams and clearing timers. runShell and runShellBytes use it (additive aborted field); add spawnManaged returning the discriminated union.",
    "size": "L",
    "order": 2,
    "acceptanceChecks": [
      "An already-aborted signal starts no process in runShell, runShellBytes or spawnManaged",
      "A descendant holding the pipes is killed and the call settles within 2 s after abort and time-out",
      "A call that is neither aborted nor timed out settles on close as before",
      "spawnManaged child is unreadable without narrowing on spawned"
